.TH devin-cloud-drs-secret-create 1  "secret-create " 
.SH NAME
devin\-cloud\-drs\-secret\-create \- Create organization\-level secrets
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBdevin cloud drs secret\-create\fR [\fB\-\-key\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-env\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-from\-dotenv\fR] [\fB\-\-stdin\fR] [\fB\-\-only\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create organization\-level secrets
.PP
Values are read by the CLI itself — from an env var, a file, a dotenv entry, or stdin — so they never appear in the command line, shell history, `ps` output, or an agent transcript.
.PP
With `\-\-key` uploads a single secret. With `\-\-from\-dotenv` and no `\-\-key`, uploads every entry of the file and prints each secret name with an ok/error status.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Secret name (omit with \-\-from\-dotenv to upload every entry)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-env\fR \fI<VAR>\fR
Read the value from this environment variable of the CLI process
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-file\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the value from this file (entire contents, trailing newline trimmed)
.TP
\fB\-\-from\-dotenv\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Read the value for `\-\-key` out of this dotenv file
.TP
\fB\-\-stdin\fR
Read the value from stdin (entire input, trailing newline trimmed)
.TP
\fB\-\-only\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Only upload these keys (repeatable; bulk dotenv mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Skip these keys (repeatable; bulk dotenv mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
List the keys that would be uploaded without uploading them
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
